    q: 'Should you do an MSc integrated PhD or a standalone MSc if you are not sure about research yet?',
    a: 'If you are genuinely unsure whether research suits you, a standalone MSc followed by a research internship, project, or a CSIR-NET/GATE attempt is usually the lower-risk route, because it keeps the PhD decision open until you have real evidence of fit. Integrated MSc-PhD programs at institutes like the IISERs or IISc suit candidates who already have strong evidence — a serious project, sustained subject excitement, or a completed internship — that the multi-year research commitment is the right one, since exiting an integrated program midway is a bigger disruption than choosing a fresh path after a standalone MSc.',
